# Polling: the client asks again on a timer. Order and Delivery Tracking can check every hour, since a
# package changes status only a handful of times a day. Every response here is what the example server
# really sends back; server/tests/test_example_files.py checks that.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Check the Delivery Status
# Expect: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/o_1001/delivery
Authorization: Bearer homeowner-token

# Response: 200 OK
# ETag: "b588d6431c467bef"
# Cache-Control: no-cache
#
# {
#   "orderId": "o_1001",
#   "status": "SHIPPED",
#   "updatedAt": "2026-11-08T09:00:00Z"
# }

### Check Again an Hour Later
# Send the ETag back as If-None-Match. Nothing changed, so the answer is 304 with no body, which is
# what keeps polling cheap.
# Expect: 304
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/o_1001/delivery
Authorization: Bearer homeowner-token
If-None-Match: "b588d6431c467bef"

# Response: 304 Not Modified
# ETag: "b588d6431c467bef"
